==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|mul|en}} ({{etyl|NL.|en}}) {{m|mul|Homo sapiens}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|sapiēns}}, present active participle of {{m|la|sapiō||discern, be capable of discerning}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sapiens}}

# [[Homo sapiens]].
#* {{quote-book|title=How we got to be human: subjective minds with objective bodies‎|page=277|author=William H. Libaw|year=2000|passage=The earliest '''sapiens''' were gatherers, scavengers, and hunters of food.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Classification and Human Evolution‎|page=335|author=Sherwood L. Washburn|year=2005|passage=Even if we assume that the rate of change was slow and the evolving population large, we must still assume that '''sapiens''' was rather isolated.}}

