==Latin==

===Etymology===
Present active participle of {{m|la|sapiō||discern, be capable of discerning}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈsa.pi.eːns/|lang=la}}

===Participle===
{{la-present participle|sapi|ens}}

# [[discerning]], [[wise]], [[judicious]]
# [[discreet]]
# {{lb|la|substantive}} a [[wise]] [[man]], [[sage]], [[philosopher]]
#* Anonymous {{rfdate}}
#*: '''Sapiens''' nihil affirmat quod non probat
#*:: "a wise man asserts nothing which he does not (ap)prove."

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-3rd-part|sapiēns}}

* ''comparative'': '''[[sapientior]]''', ''superlative'': '''[[sapientissimus]]'''

